  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted (config_026, acc=0.7250) is the best configuration, with concat fusion (config_016, acc=0.7207) nearly matching it. The only aggregation tested with this top encoder pair is 'transformer'. Config_047 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) isolates the aggregation method while holding the best-known encoders and fusion fixed. This tells us whether the transformer aggregation is a critical contributor or whether a simpler avgpool suffices—reducing uncertainty about a key architectural dimension. If avgpool performs comparably, we free up design flexibility; if it degrades significantly, we confirm transformer aggregation is essential and can focus remaining budget on other axes (e.g., profile setting or alternative RNA encoders). With 5 experiments left, this minimal-change test is the highest-information next step before committing to further exploitation."
